fake_id0: pass uid_map reads to the kernel; translate SO_PEERCRED across instances

Read-only opens of /proc/<pid|self>/{uid_map,gid_map,setgroups} were
redirected to /dev/null along with writes, so readers saw an empty map,
meaning "user namespace without a mapping". Tools that verify file and
socket ownership then refuse to run (Claude Code's background daemon).
Only redirect opens for writing.

SO_PEERCRED was only rewritten for peers traced by the same PRoot, so
apps running one PRoot per terminal saw peers in other terminals with
the real uid while getuid() returned the fake one. Report a peer with
PRoot's real uid using the caller's fake ids.

Upstream as termux/proot b5af02e (#406), which no release has yet; drop
this once PROOT is past it.

diff --git a/src/extension/fake_id0/getsockopt.c b/src/extension/fake_id0/getsockopt.c
index e0874b4..1977f13 100644
--- a/src/extension/fake_id0/getsockopt.c
+++ b/src/extension/fake_id0/getsockopt.c
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 #include <sys/socket.h>  /* SOL_SOCKET,SO_PEERCRED */
+#include <unistd.h>      /* getuid(2) */
 
 #include "tracee/reg.h"
 #include "tracee/mem.h"
@@ -33,6 +34,11 @@ int handle_getsockopt_exit_end(Tracee *tracee) {
 		int status = read_data(tracee, &cred, cred_addr, sizeof(struct ucred));
 		if (status) return 0;
 		Config *peer_config = get_fake_id_for_pid(cred.pid);
+		/* A peer under another PRoot instance (or none) that runs
+		 * as our real uid is the same user: report it with this
+		 * tracee's own fake ids, as the tracee's getuid() does.  */
+		if (peer_config == NULL && cred.uid == getuid())
+			peer_config = get_fake_id_for_pid(tracee->pid);
 		if (peer_config == NULL) return 0;
 		cred.uid = peer_config->euid;
 		cred.gid = peer_config->egid;
